{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123902","id":4659905858,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFcCFQg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123902","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123902.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123902.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123902","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123902/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123902/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123902/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/92fc4aa9521c6916c382292d490b452ca3239891","number":123902,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"🤖 Web: Handle text from input methods that don't compose","user":{"login":"denis00001232","id":49843085,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODQzMDg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49843085?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232","html_url":"https://github.com/denis00001232","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denis00001232/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!INFO] *AI disclosure*: This contribution was authored by an autonomous AI agent (Claude Code), on behalf of a user, to fix text input in their Godot web export. The agent diagnosed the issue, wrote the patch and this description; the user tested the fix in their browser.\n\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\nOn the web platform, text typed through an input method that commits characters directly (without composition events) never reaches `LineEdit`/`TextEdit`. No existing issue found.\n\n**Reproduction:** Ubuntu (GNOME, Wayland) with IBus and a Russian layout, Chrome or Firefox, any web export with a focused `LineEdit`: Latin letters type, Cyrillic letters don't. The browser sends `keydown` with `key == \"Process\"` (`keyCode == 229`) and delivers the character only in an `input` event (`inputType == \"insertText\"`) on the focused IME element. Most mobile virtual keyboards use the same pattern.\n\n## Additional information\n\n**Cause:** the IME element (`GodotIME`) forwards every keydown to the engine (as the raw key `\"Process\"`, which carries no unicode), calls `preventDefault()`, and only listens to composition events, so the text is dropped.\n\n**Fix:** keydowns that belong to the input method (`isComposing`, `keyCode == 229`, `\"Process\"`, `\"Unidentified\"`) are left to the browser, and `insertText` input events are committed like a finished composition (start + commit), which `DisplayServerWeb` already turns into unicode key events. Normal keys and composition-based IMEs should be unaffected.\n\n**Tested:** a 4.7.1-based web export (a minimal project with `LineEdit` + `TextEdit`) on Ubuntu (GNOME, Wayland) with IBus: Cyrillic now types; and on a phone browser with its virtual keyboard: Latin and Cyrillic typing and Backspace work. **Not tested:** CJK IMEs.\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":f